{
  "dom_id": "step-e5060",
  "name": "Example: Solving an Elementary Quadratic Inequality Using the Absolute Value Method",
  "problem": "Solve the inequality $x^2 \\leq 2$ using the absolute value method.",
  "worked_solution": "Taking the square root of both sides of the inequality, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & \\le 2 \\\\ \\sqrt{{x}^{2}} & \\le \\sqrt{2} \\\\ |x| & \\le \\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the definition of absolute value, we must have\n\n$$\n-\\sqrt 2\\leq x \\leq \\sqrt 2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x \\in [-\\sqrt 2,\\sqrt 2].$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "result": null,
